<title>USA: Consolidated Stores Q1 net loss.</title>
<headline>Consolidated Stores Q1 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>						 Thirteen weeks ended</p>
<p>				     May 3,	 May 4,	  May 4,</p>
<p>					1997	   1996(a)	  1996</p>
<p>    Net sales		    594.9	   498.4	   322.0</p>
<p>    Operating profit (loss)  ($7.3)	 ($15.5)	  $10.4</p>
<p>    Net income (loss)	  ($7.3)	 ($14.1)	   $3.6</p>
<p>    Net income (loss) shr    ($0.10)	($0.20)	  $0.06</p>
<p>    Weighted avg shrs	   70.1	    68.7	    62.3</p>
<p>(a)  Pro forma results reflecting acquisition of Kay-Bee Toys at the beginning of fiscal 1996. Pro forma presentation includes the effect of certain purchase adjustments directly attributable to the acquisition which are expected to have a continuing impact.</p>
<p>The company said it had record Q1 sales, which rose 84.8 percent from a year ago. Comparable store sales for stores open two years rose 9.5 percent from a year ago.</p>
</text>
